<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.hermes.cron.plist.template — launchd host for the Phase 3C Cron loop.

  This SUPERSEDES com.hermes.dream.plist.template: instead of launchd knowing
  about one hardcoded job (Dream), launchd hosts the generic cron loop and
  the loop reads its jobs from cron/cron.db (add them with
  `python3 cron/scheduler.py add ...`). Migrate by unloading com.hermes.dream
  and adding Dream as a cron job:
      python3 cron/scheduler.py add dream "python3 mnemos/dream.py" --daily 03:30

  Replace __HERMES_ROOT__ with the absolute repo path before loading
  (docs/SCHEDULING.md has a one-liner that does it for you).

  Replace __PYTHON_BIN__ with an EXPLICIT absolute python3 path (e.g.
  `$(which python3)` from the shell you actually use) — NOT `/usr/bin/env
  python3`. Found live 2026-07-10: `env` resolves python3 via launchd's own
  minimal PATH, which can silently land on a DIFFERENT binary than the one
  you use interactively (e.g. `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/python3`
  instead of a venv's python3). Since the repo lives under `~/Documents`
  (TCC-protected), that resolved binary needs Full Disk Access, and if you
  can't see/control which binary `env` picked, you end up granting access
  to the wrong one and the loop fails with "Operation not permitted"
  forever with no further hint. Pinning an explicit path removes the
  ambiguity — see docs/SCHEDULING.md.

  Invariant #7: Cowork cannot host this loop — launchd on the CLI box is the
  production scheduler. KeepAlive restarts the loop if it dies; the loop's
  .tick.lock makes an overlapping restart harmless (one tick wins).

  Replace __PATH__ with your interactive shell's $PATH (docs/SCHEDULING.md
  has the one-liner). Found live 2026-07-11: delegation/agenda.py's tick()
  spawns children via the literal argv[0] "claude", resolved by PATH lookup
  at call time (dispatch.claude_cli_available() = shutil.which("claude")).
  launchd's own minimal PATH does NOT include wherever `claude` actually
  lives (nvm/npm-global/homebrew/etc — wherever your interactive shell
  finds it). Without this key, claude_cli_available() returns False on
  every tick forever, tick() returns early before touching the agenda, and
  exits 0 anyway (no sys.exit(1) on that path) — so the scheduler logs
  "completed" over and over while the agenda sits at attempts:0 with no
  error anywhere. Exact same PATH-inside-launchd-is-not-PATH-in-your-shell
  class of bug as __PYTHON_BIN__ above, hitting a different binary.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.hermes.cron</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>__PYTHON_BIN__</string>
        <string>__HERMES_ROOT__/cron/scheduler.py</string>
        <string>loop</string>
        <string>--poll</string>
        <string>60</string>
    </array>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>__HERMES_ROOT__/logs/cron_launchd.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>__HERMES_ROOT__/logs/cron_launchd.log</string>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>__HERMES_ROOT__</string>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>__PATH__</string>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
